.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-SELF-UPDATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-self-update
.Nd fetch the latest nomad script
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad self-update
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad self-update
fetches the latest version of the
.Nm nomad
script from the project repository and replaces the installed copy in place. It
also refreshes the companion
.Pa compose.yaml
so the CLI and the compose file stay in sync.
.Pp
The update is conservative. It is skipped silently when the machine is offline,
when the bundle is a git working copy (so a developer's checkout is never
overwritten), or when the fetched script is identical to the current one. The
download is validated as a bash script and syntax-checked before it replaces
the live file; on any failure the current version is kept. When a newer script
is installed, the command re-executes with the new version.
.Pp
The same self-update runs automatically at the start of
.Ic nomad install
and
.Ic nomad reinstall .
This command is the way to refresh on demand without reinstalling.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad self-update
Pull the latest nomad script and compose file, then report whether an update
was applied.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-install 1 ,
.Xr nomad-reinstall 1
